# EVERYTHING IN THIS REPO RUNS UNDER LINUX, so everything in it is checked out LF.
#
# This catch-all is FIRST on purpose: later rules win in .gitattributes, so the
# binary pins below still override it.
#
# core.autocrlf is `true` on this Windows checkout. Without this line git rewrites
# every tracked text file to CRLF on checkout, and bash cannot read a CRLF script.
# The failure is not loud - it is worse than loud. `. dashboard/testlib.sh` dies with
#
#     syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
#
# which means ok(), bad(), check() and finish() never get defined; every assertion in
# every suite that sources it then evaporates as "command not found", the pass and
# fail counters stay at zero, and the suite runs to the end and exits 127 having
# verified nothing. A harness that cannot fail is the one thing this repo keeps
# deciding it will not ship.
#
# run_tests.sh already works around this per-suite (`bash <(tr -d '\r' < ...)`), which
# is why it went unnoticed: the workaround covers the file being INVOKED and not the
# files it sources. Fix the bytes instead of adding a second workaround.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The preserved gateway bytecode is the ONLY surviving copy of a lost source file
# (see taskmgmt/recovered/README.md). Git's auto-detection gets this right today,
# but this checkout is on a Windows drive and a core.autocrlf setting on some other
# machine would rewrite line endings inside the file and silently corrupt it - and a
# corrupt .pyc cannot be recompiled, because there is no source. Pin it explicitly.
taskmgmt/recovered/*.bin binary
*.pyc                    binary
*.png                    binary
*.gz                     binary

# Every other binary shape that lives in this tree. A packet capture is the reason
# this list is explicit rather than left to auto-detection: a CR-stripping pass over
# the working tree silently removed 22 bytes from nettraffic/fixtures/sample.pcap,
# because a .pcap looks enough like text to be mangled and nothing like text once it
# has been. text=auto guesses; these do not.
*.pcap                   binary
*.jpg                    binary
*.jpeg                   binary
*.ico                    binary
*.woff                   binary
*.woff2                  binary
*.zip                    binary
*.db                     binary
